timestamp=2026-11-04T13:20:16.520Z level=INFO run=f66adc04 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/synthetic_stroke_data.csv')\ndf = df.copy()\n\nmask_valid = (df['avg_glucose_level'] >= 20) & (df['avg_glucose_level'] <= 800) & \\\n             (df['bmi'] >= 10) & (df['bmi'] <= 60) & \\\n             (df['age'] <= 120)\ndf_valid = df[mask_valid].copy()\n\n# 2. Outlier detection using 3*IQR method\n# Start with identifying outliers by IQR on all numeric variables? Or just per variable as stated?\n# \"Next, perform outlier detection using the 3*IQR method.\"\n# Apply to numeric variables (age, bmi, avg_glucose_level). Each variable separately?\noutlier_indices = set()\n\n# For each numeric column\nfor col in ['age', 'bmi', 'avg_glucose_level']:\n    q1 = df_valid[col].quantile(0.25)\n    q3 = df_valid[col].quantile(0.75)\n    iqr = q3 - q1\n    lower = q1 - 3*iqr\n    upper = q3 + 3*iqr\n    mask_out = (df_valid[col] < lower) | (df_valid[col] > upper)\n    outlier_indices.update(df_valid[mask_out].index.tolist())\n\nprint('IQR outliers (any var):', len(outlier_indices))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
