timestamp=2026-11-04T13:37:54.757Z level=INFO run=f66adc04 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Collect all categorical outliers\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/synthetic_stroke_data.csv')\ncat_outliers = set()\n\n# toddlers that are students\nmask = (df['age'] <= 3) & (df['work_type'] == 'student')\nfor idx in df[mask].index:\n    cat_outliers.add(idx)\n\n# toddlers smoking\nmask = (df['age'] <= 3) & (df['smoking_status'].isin(['smokes', 'formerly smoked']))\nfor idx in df[mask].index:\n    cat_outliers.add(idx)\n\n# children (age <= 14) smoking or formerly smoked - is this considered an outlier per the instruction?\n# The instruction says \"values among the categorical variables that are unlikely in reality...\" and gives examples.\n# It’s plausible these are considered outliers in this context. Let us include them to be safe.\nmask = (df['age'] <= 14) & (df['smoking_status'].isin(['smokes', 'formerly smoked']))\nfor idx in df[mask].index:\n    cat_outliers.add(idx)\n\nprint(len(cat_outliers))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
